## Key Takeaways from the Generated Report

* Why Snowflake Schema fails here: To load your detailed view matching a party's age, city, and market value alongside employee and branch details, a Snowflake schema forces the database engine into a chain join (Fact → Party → City → Region). At 200 million rows, this causes data shuffling across server nodes, killing your sub-second dashboard performance.
* Why a Flat Table fails here: While computing a quick SUM(Market_Value) is fast on a flat table, calculating COUNT(DISTINCT Employee) forces a brutal, memory-heavy de-duplication scan over millions of duplicate string fields. A Star Schema maintains small, indexable unique keys instead.

